      "id": 1,
      "text": "Glenwood means \"valley of trees,\" derived from the Old English words glenn and wudu.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/glenwood-45283",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village traces back to mid‑19th century settlers who farmed the area before it evolved into a suburban community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/glenwood-45283",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Glenwood officially incorporated as a village in 1939, marking its formal municipal status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/glenwood-45283",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The ancient Glenwood Shoreline, a remnant of Lake Chicago, runs through the village’s northern edge.",
